<?php
/**
 * "المنتجات المفضلة" — the wishlist. Figma 817:18852, card 821:17006.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * THE ROW IS THE ORDER CARD, NOT A NEW COMPONENT
 * ===========================================================================
 * 821:17006 is an instance of Figma's "Card - Order History" component, the
 * same one the order-history card (562:17887) is. Its Main Container, its
 * 96x96 Image Container, its Heading/H4 name and its brand-coloured price are
 * the same nodes with the same metrics, so this template emits
 * `.spartrak-order-card` and its existing `__items` / `__item` / `__thumb` /
 * `__item-content` parts. Two modifiers cover the differences: the card has no
 * `__head` here, and `__foot--actions-only` puts the buttons at the reading
 * end because there are no facts to sit opposite them.
 *
 * Building a `.spartrak-wishlist-card` instead would have been a second copy
 * of a component the design does not fork — see the layout file, and
 * CLAUDE.md §2 step 4.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * THE SAVE PATHS ARE MAGENTO'S, DOWN TO THE SELECTORS
 * ===========================================================================
 * `data-mage-init` on the form is core's, verbatim, and so are the two
 * controls' hooks:
 *
 *   [data-role=tocart] + data-post   -> mage.wishlist._beforeAddToCart, which
 *                                       then posts through mage/dataPost
 *   [data-role=remove] + data-post-remove
 *                                    -> mage.wishlist's own click handler
 *
 * Both attribute values come from `Magento\Wishlist\Block\AbstractBlock`
 * (getItemAddToCartParams / getItemRemoveParams), i.e. the same signed post
 * payloads core's own templates emit. So add-to-cart, the minicart update, the
 * success message and the CSRF key are all the platform's, and this feature
 * ships no controller and no JavaScript of its own.
 *
 * NO `qty` INPUT, and that is safe: `_beforeAddToCart` reads
 * `[name="qty[<id>]"]`, gets `undefined` when there is none, and `$.extend`
 * drops undefined values — so the post carries no qty and the server uses the
 * item's own. Figma draws no quantity control.
 *
 * `#form-tmpl` is NOT carried over from core's view.phtml. It is read only by
 * the gift-registry extension of the widget, via
 * `[data-wishlist-to-giftregistry]`, which Magento Open Source never renders.
 *
 * REMOVAL IS IMMEDIATE, as in core — no confirm dialog, because Figma draws
 * none and inventing one would be inventing UI (§3). The action is
 * recoverable: the product is one click from being re-added.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * READING ORDER IS DOM ORDER
 * ===========================================================================
 * This document is `dir="rtl"`, so the FIRST child of a flex row sits at the
 * right. Figma's row draws the image at the right and the buttons at the left,
 * so the image is written first and حذف is written before شراء الآن. That is
 * what mirrors correctly for the English store view with no second stylesheet
 * (§16) — the same rule the order-history template documents.
 *
 * @var \Magento\Wishlist\Block\Customer\Wishlist $block
 * @var \Magento\Framework\Escaper $escaper
 */

use Magento\Framework\Exception\LocalizedException;
use Magento\Wishlist\Helper\Data as WishlistHelper;
use Spartrak\Wishlist\ViewModel\WishlistItem;

/** @var WishlistItem|null $wishlistItem */
$wishlistItem = $block->getData('wishlist_item');

// Core's own gate: a store with the wishlist switched off renders nothing at
// all rather than an empty card for a feature that is not on.
if (!$this->helper(WishlistHelper::class)->isAllow()) {
    return;
}

$items = $block->hasWishlistItems() ? $block->getWishlistItems() : [];

/*
 * A wiring fault, not an empty wishlist — and the two must not look the same.
 * `wishlist_item` is supplied by this theme's wishlist_index_index.xml; if it
 * did not arrive, that layout file was not applied, which also means the four
 * `remove="true"` directives in it were not applied either. Rendering the empty
 * state here would tell a shopper with a full wishlist that they have nothing
 * saved. Throwing gets Magento's error page with a report id instead, and this
 * branch is unreachable on a correctly wired store. Same argument, at more
 * length, in Spartrak_CustomerAccount::order/view.phtml.
 */
if ($items !== [] && $wishlistItem === null) {
    throw new LocalizedException(
        __(
            'This wishlist is misconfigured: the `wishlist_item` argument did not reach '
            . '`customer.wishlist`, so this theme\'s Magento_Wishlist/layout/wishlist_index_index.xml '
            . 'was not applied.'
        )
    );
}

/*
 * ===========================================================================
 * THE PAGER, AND THE FOUR THINGS IT SHIPS THAT FIGMA DOES NOT DRAW
 * ===========================================================================
 * Configured here rather than from the layout file on purpose: core's
 * Magento\Wishlist\Block\Customer\Wishlist::_prepareLayout() calls
 * `->setUseContainer(true)->setShowAmounts(true)` on this exact block, and
 * _prepareLayout runs while the layout is being generated. A layout `<action>`
 * would win (actions run after generation) but it would be the ONLY pager on
 * the site configured that way — the PLP's toolbar.phtml and the order list's
 * history.phtml both do it here, and one pattern beats a clever one.
 *
 * THE FLAGS ARE MAGENTO'S OWN IDIOM FOR A BARE PAGINATION CONTROL, not a local
 * invention: Catalog\Block\Product\ProductList\Toolbar::getPagerHtml() calls
 * `setUseContainer(false)->setShowPerPage(false)->setShowAmounts(false)` on its
 * pager for exactly this reason.
 *
 *   AMOUNTS      "%1 Item(s)" — which rendered as "Item(s) 2" in English on
 *                this store, and is not in Figma's pagination (569:14143)
 *                in any language. Off.
 *   PER PAGE     the "عرض [10] لكل صفحة" limiter. Not in 569:14143 either; the
 *                PLP records the same omission for the same reason.
 *   CONTAINER    core's own `<div class="pager">` wrapper. This template
 *                supplies the wrapper (with the component class on it), and
 *                leaving core's on as well would emit an empty div on a
 *                single-page wishlist — which is every wishlist under eleven
 *                items.
 *   ANCHOR TEXT  without it core marks the prev/next controls `class="action"`,
 *                which Porto styles as an icon-font glyph with the label
 *                hidden; with the glyph unavailable that renders as a blank
 *                box. Setting the text switches core to `class="link"` and
 *                gives the pill the word Figma draws.
 */
$pager = $block->getChildBlock('wishlist_item_pager');

if ($pager) {
    $pager->setShowAmounts(false)
        ->setShowPerPage(false)
        ->setUseContainer(false)
        ->setAnchorTextForPrevious(__('Previous'))
        ->setAnchorTextForNext(__('Next'));
}

$pagerHtml = $block->getChildHtml('wishlist_item_pager');
?>
<div class="spartrak-account-card">
    <div class="spartrak-account-card__header">
        <div class="spartrak-account-card__heading">
            <h1 class="spartrak-account-card__title">
                <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Favourite products')) ?>
            </h1>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="spartrak-account-card__body spartrak-account-card__body--tight">
        <?php /*
          The form wraps the ROWS, so an empty wishlist renders no form at all
          rather than an empty one: nothing to submit, no `wishlist` widget to
          mount, one fewer hidden form-key input on the page.
        */ ?>
        <?php if ($items !== []) : ?>
        <form class="form-wishlist-items spartrak-wishlist"
              id="wishlist-view-form"
              action="<?= $escaper->escapeUrl($block->getUrl(
                  'wishlist/index/update',
                  ['wishlist_id' => $block->getWishlistInstance()->getId()]
              )) ?>"
              method="post"
              data-mage-init='{"wishlist":{
                  "addToCartUrl":<?= /* @noEscape */ $block->getItemAddToCartParams('%item%') ?>,
                  "addAllToCartUrl":<?= /* @noEscape */ $block->getAddAllToCartParams() ?>,
                  "commentString":""},
                  "validation": {}}'>
            <?= $block->getBlockHtml('formkey') ?>

            <ul class="spartrak-wishlist__list">
                <?php foreach ($items as $item) : ?>
                    <?php
                    $product = $item->getProduct();

                    if ($product === null || !$product->getId()) {
                        // The product was deleted after it was saved. Core's
                        // collection filters by visibility, not existence, so
                        // this is reachable — and a row with no name, no price
                        // and a buy button that 404s is worse than no row.
                        continue;
                    }

                    $image = $wishlistItem->getItemImage($item);
                    ?>
                    <li class="spartrak-order-card" data-row="product-item">
                        <div class="spartrak-order-card__items">
                            <div class="spartrak-order-card__item">
                                <span class="spartrak-order-card__thumb">
                                    <?php if ($image !== null) : ?>
                                        <img src="<?= $escaper->escapeUrl($image->getUrl()) ?>"
                                             alt=""
                                             width="<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr($image->getWidth()) ?>"
                                             height="<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr($image->getHeight()) ?>"
                                             loading="lazy"
                                             decoding="async">
                                    <?php endif; ?>
                                </span>
                                <div class="spartrak-order-card__item-content">
                                    <p class="spartrak-order-card__item-name">
                                        <a href="<?= $escaper->escapeUrl($block->getProductUrl($item)) ?>">
                                            <?= $escaper->escapeHtml($product->getName()) ?>
                                        </a>
                                    </p>
                                    <p class="spartrak-order-card__item-price">
                                        <?php /*
                                          The platform's pricing pipeline, through
                                          AbstractBlock::getItemPriceHtml() — so a configurable or
                                          bundle row prints the price of what was actually saved,
                                          and the theme's own final_price.phtml override (with its
                                          "price on request" fallback for a zero price) applies
                                          here as it does everywhere else.
                                        */ ?>
                                        <?= /* @noEscape */ $block->getItemPriceHtml($item) ?>
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="spartrak-order-card__foot spartrak-order-card__foot--actions-only">
                            <div class="spartrak-order-card__actions">
                                <button type="button"
                                        class="spartrak-order-card__remove"
                                        data-role="remove"
                                        data-post-remove='<?= /* @noEscape */ $block->getItemRemoveParams($item) ?>'>
                                    <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Delete')) ?>
                                </button>
                                <?php if ($wishlistItem->isBuyable($item)) : ?>
                                    <button type="button"
                                            class="spartrak-order-card__buy"
                                            data-role="tocart"
                                            data-item-id="<?= $escaper->escapeHtmlAttr($item->getId()) ?>"
                                            data-post='<?= /* @noEscape */ $block->getItemAddToCartParams($item) ?>'>
                                        <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Buy now')) ?>
                                    </button>
                                <?php endif; ?>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                <?php endforeach; ?>
            </ul>

            <?php if (trim((string) $pagerHtml) !== '') : ?>
                <?php /*
                  `spartrak-pagination` is the shared control — the same
                  component the PLP and the order list use
                  (components/_pagination.less). Trimmed rather than tested
                  truthily because a single-page pager emits whitespace,
                  not nothing, and an empty wrapper would still take the
                  list's 24px gap.
                */ ?>
                <div class="spartrak-wishlist__pager spartrak-pagination">
                    <?= /* @noEscape */ $pagerHtml ?>
                </div>
            <?php endif; ?>
        </form>
        <?php else : ?>
            <?php /*
              ===================================================================
              THE EMPTY WISHLIST — Figma 1179:10687, container 1179:10948
              ===================================================================
              The storefront's shared empty state, third caller
              (components/_empty-state.less): `--panel` is this frame's
              bg/surface-subtle box with its 12/12/26 padding, and the base 16px
              gap is what 1179:10948 draws — the address book's 26 is the
              outlier, not this.

              WHAT WAS HERE: core's own sentence, "You have no items in your
              wish list.", in a bare <p>. No illustration, no way out, and in
              English on an Arabic store because nothing had ever translated it.

              THE CTA IS THE NAVY ONE, and that is read off the node
              (1179:11035 → action/primary with action/primary-text), not off
              its layer name — the cart and the address book both call their
              quiet bg/field control "Primary Buttons" too. `__action--primary`
              is the modifier that says so.

              WHERE IT GOES: the storefront root. Figma's `الذهاب للتسوق`
              names shopping in general, not a category, and this store's
              landing page is where the collections it mentions are. `getUrl('')`
              rather than a hardcoded '/' so the store code and the secure base
              URL are Magento's to decide.
            */ ?>
            <div class="spartrak-empty-state spartrak-empty-state--panel">
                <span class="spartrak-empty-state__art spartrak-empty-state__art--wishlist"
                      aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <div class="spartrak-empty-state__copy">
                    <p class="spartrak-empty-state__title">
                        <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('You have no favourite products!')) ?>
                    </p>
                    <p class="spartrak-empty-state__text">
                        <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(
                            __('Start now by adding your favourite products, shopping from our own collections!')
                        ) ?>
                    </p>
                    <a class="spartrak-empty-state__action spartrak-empty-state__action--primary"
                       href="<?= $escaper->escapeUrl($block->getUrl('')) ?>">
                        <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Go shopping')) ?>
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>
        <?php endif; ?>
    </div>
</div>
